-- title:
--   Finite level sets become closed subschemes after base change
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $C$ a scheme and $c\colon C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a separated morphism. Let $U_0 \subseteq C$ be an open subscheme which is affine, let $f \in \Gamma(C, U_0)$, let $S$ be an $R$-algebra and $s \in S$. Here $\Gamma(C, U_0)$ carries the $R$-algebra structure `Scheme.TwoAffineOpenCover.algebraOfHom` coming from the ring map $R \to \Gamma(C,U_0)$ induced by $c$ (the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ adjunction isomorphism for $R$ followed by the restriction $c^{\#}$ from $\top$ to $U_0$). Write $B = (S \otimes_R \Gamma(C,U_0))/I$ with $I$ the ideal generated by $1 \otimes f - s \otimes 1$, and assume $B$ is a finite $S$-module. The conclusion asserts the existence of a morphism $\iota\colon \operatorname{Spec} B \to C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} S$, where the fibre product is taken along $c$ and along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R \to S$, such that $\iota$ is a closed immersion and $\iota$ followed by the second projection $C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} S \to \operatorname{Spec} S$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $S \to B$; that is, $\iota$ is a closed immersion over $\operatorname{Spec} S$.
--
--   This realises the level set $\{f = s\}$ inside the base change $C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} S$ as a closed subscheme, under the sole assumption that the level-set ring is module-finite over $S$: finiteness prevents the locus from meeting the boundary of the chart $U_0$. It is used in the construction of finite étale charts for sections of relative Picard schemes and of smooth proper curves, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.exists_finite_etale_hasChartSections_of_field`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.exists_finite_etale_hasChartSections_of_field) and [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_finite_etale_isClosedImmersion_le_finrank_of_finiteMapData`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_finite_etale_isClosedImmersion_le_finrank_of_finiteMapData).
